    "text": "If the differential equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math> is satisfied by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></math> (where&nbsp;<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></math> is an arbitrary constant), then the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi></math> is",
